  "intermediates": [],
  "extraction_notes": "This figure shows a substrate scope for amide bond formation using DATB 8a catalyst. The generic reaction uses carboxylic acid 10 + amine 11 to form amides. The DATB 8a catalyst structure is not drawn in this figure (only referenced by label). Some structural assignments are uncertain: (1) For compound 19, the chain length between NH and OTBS was estimated as 3 CH2 groups. (2) For compound 21, the ring was interpreted as tetrahydropyran (oxane) based on drawing. (3) For compound 22, interpreted as 4-fluorobenzoyl based on F substituent visible on the ring. (4) For compound 26, the amine 11g was interpreted as (1H-indol-5-yl)methylamine. (5) For compound 27, the acid was interpreted as cyclopentanecarboxylic acid and amine 11h as 2-aminobenzimidazole. (6) For compound 28, the acid was interpreted as benzo[b]thiophene-2-carboxylic acid."
}